{"name":"Foothills","hex":"#e1cfa5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"foothills","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of foothill"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foothills"}],"entries":[{"title":"Foothills","blocks":[{"text":"Foothills or piedmont are geographically defined as gradual increases in elevation at the base of a mountain range, higher hill range or an upland area. They are a transition zone between plains and low relief hills and the adjacent topographically higher mountains, hills, and uplands. Frequently foothills consist of alluvial fans, coalesced alluvial fans, and dissected plateaus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Foothillsco.JPG/330px-Foothillsco.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foothills"},{"title":"Foothills (electoral district)","blocks":[{"text":"Foothills is a federal electoral district in Alberta, Canada, that has been represented in the House of Commons of Canada since 2015."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foothills_(electoral_district)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Prospect_Hill.jpg/500px-Prospect_Hill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Prospect_Hill.jpg/1280px-Prospect_Hill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Prospect_Hill.jpg/500px-Prospect_Hill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Foothills of Prospect Hill, New South Wales, Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProspect_Hill.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Enate Somontano 2017","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Enate_Somontano_2017.jpg/500px-Enate_Somont